                                "sense_id": "ddb500e5-bac0-3367-8317-eab487272441",
                                "text": "Then followed Talmudism in such parts of Jewdom as had become European."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f0cef90b-5e90-4822-aeff-5529ad4af21c",
                                "sense_id": "ddb500e5-bac0-3367-8317-eab487272441",
                                "text": "The peculiar Morality of Jewdom. That the Hebrew is not very particular with regard to his moral obligations towards other people, is fairly well known."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fab49ab9-cb31-3d5f-a535-57347d9eefd1",
                        "entry_id": "0a6e4447-9baf-3599-b718-fb01b1e42bf7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The state or condition of being a Jew; Jewishness."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rare",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "621aaca5-6f5d-4822-aef1-41650d43f80c",
                                "sense_id": "fab49ab9-cb31-3d5f-a535-57347d9eefd1",
                                "text": "The self-emancipation of our age would be emancipation from bargaining and from money, that is from practical, real Jewdom."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
